<p>The first edition of the <a href="https://archive.org/details/collins-cobuild-english-language-dictionary_202603/mode/2up?q=%22If+you+hink%2C+you+think%22"><em>Collins COBUILD English Language Dictionary</em></a> (1987) contains a fictitious entry, presumably to catch content thieves:</p>
<p><b>hink, hinks, hinking, hinked.</b> If you <b>hink</b>, you think hopefully and unrealistically about something.</p>
<p>Phony or not, this is a useful word. If it&#8217;s adopted widely enough, perhaps the dictionary entry will bootstrap itself into legitimacy.</p>
